      "text": "Gallo Lab About Gallo Lab Gallo Lab Focus Our research is focused on understanding how the skin and its resident microbiome defends the body against infections and the environment. We apply modern techniques of biochemistry, immunology, microbiology, and genetics to study complex biological systems within the immune system and the microbiome. Our goal is to translate this information into improved diagnostics and therapeutics to better understand and treat human disease. Publications The Team The Gallo Lab team is made up of a group of dedicated researchers from around the world. Meet us Publications Featured publications in Science, Nature, Nature Medicine, Science Translational Medicine, Immunity and more. Our featured articles Gallo Lab in the News March 2021 Using the Skin Microbiome to Control Atopic Dermatitis More on the Skin Microbiome February 2021 Last-Itch Effort: Fighting the Bacteria That Exacerbate Eczema with Bacteria More on bacteria and eczema October 2020 Acne Yields Up Secret That Points to New Treatments More on new treatments Contact us Phone: 858-82 2-4608 Email: prushton@ucsd.edu Address: 9500 Gilman Drive, Mail Code 0869, La Jolla, CA 92093-0869 Location: 9452 Medical Center Drive, La Jolla, CA 92037 Map: Altman CTRI Building More information",
